# A dialogue that opens on its own when a player finishes loading in: the only driver for the on.join check.
#
# No npc: directive, because it has no NPC -- that is the point of on: join -- so speaker: names the voice.
#
# It opens once per player and then stops. A window that reappeared on every login for ever would be a
# nuisance long after it had proved its point, and the check is a one-off by nature.
#
# Gated on visited() rather than the harness's own checked(): the harness marks on.join from the opener while
# the dialogue is still opening, so checked("on.join") is already true by the time this passage is read and
# the window would never show at all. visited() answers about a passage, which is only reached once the
# window is really up.

title: LowTalk harness: joined
speaker: Harness
on: join

== start
<<if visited("check_on_join")>>
    <<end>>
<<endif>>
<<jump check_on_join>>

== check_on_join
This opened by itself when you finished loading in, with no NPC and nothing clicked: that is the whole of the on.join check. It will not open again for you.
<<end>>
